-- title:
--   Effectiveness of a descent datum is local on the base
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a category with pullbacks and let $F$ be a pseudofunctor from the locally discrete bicategory on $C^{\mathrm{op}}$ to $\mathbf{Cat}$, so that each $g \colon Z' \to Z$ in $C$ induces a functor $g^{*} \colon F(Z) \to F(Z')$. Let $P$ be a predicate on the objects of the fibres $F(Z)$, assumed stable under every such $g^{*}$ (hypothesis `hP`) and under isomorphism, in the form that $P(M)$ and $\mathrm{Nonempty}(M \cong N)$ imply $P(N)$ (hypothesis `hP'`). Let $f \colon X \to S$ be a morphism, and let $u_i \colon U_i \to S$ be a family of morphisms indexed by a type $\iota$. Assume: $F$ is a stack for the presieve generated by the arrows $u_i$; for every $z \colon Z \to S$, $F$ is a prestack for the presieve generated by the base-changed arrows $\mathrm{pr}_1 \colon Z \times_S U_i \to Z$; and for every $z \colon Z \to S$ and all objects $M, N$ of $F(Z)$ satisfying $P$, the functor `F.toDescentData` from $F(Z)$ to descent data along the one-element family $\mathrm{pr}_2 \colon X \times_S Z \to Z$ acts bijectively on $\mathrm{Hom}(M,N)$. Let $D$ be a descent datum for $F$ along the one-element (indexed by `Unit`) family $f$, and suppose for each $i$ there is an object $L_i$ of $F(U_i)$ with $P(L_i)$ whose associated descent datum along $\mathrm{pr}_2 \colon X \times_S U_i \to U_i$ is isomorphic to the pullback of $D$ along $u_i$, taken with `DescentData.pullFunctor` for the cartesian square expressed by `pullback.condition`. Then there exists an object $L$ of $F(S)$ such that $P(u_i^{*}L)$ for every $i$ and the descent datum associated with $L$ along $f$ is isomorphic to $D$.
--
--   This is the statement that effectiveness of a descent datum is local on the base: local solutions over a cover, unique up to unique isomorphism by the fully faithfulness hypothesis, glue to a global object by the stack and prestack hypotheses. It is applied to the pseudofunctor of modules on schemes, in the effectivity result for descent data of invertible modules along a flat surjective affine morphism.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CategoryTheory_Pseudofunctor_DescentData_exists_iso_toDescentData_obj_of_isStackFor_of_forall_exists_iso_pullFunctor_obj.lean

